OL,3,GNEWSATeen thanks Children in Need for
OL,4,Aholiday club
OL,5,
OL,6,FA teenage girl from Bramhall has
OL,7,Fthanked BBC Children in Need for
OL,8,Fhelping to fund a school holiday club
OL,9,Ffor students with learning
OL,10,Fdifficulties.
OL,12,FThe Children's Activities and Disabled
OL,13,FSports (CADS) programme is run by
OL,14,FStockport-based charity the Seashell
OL,15,FTrust.
OL,17,FGrace, who has cerebral palsy, said she
OL,18,Fdoes "bikes, drumming and swimming" at
OL,19,Fthe sessions, adding: "Without it, I'd
OL,20,Fjust chill around the house."
